<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=pound-lock">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Building and engineering</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pound lock</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">984</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A pound lock is a chamber with gates at both ends in which the water level is raised or lowered to move boats between levels of a waterway, first built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> by Qiao Weiyue in 984. He placed two sluice gates 250 feet apart under a roof, replacing double slipways, at one of which soldiers had plotted with bandits to wreck grain barges. On the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a> such locks raised the water level by 138 feet. The first true European pound lock was built at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damme">Damme</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a> in 1396.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pound-lock.jpg" alt="Pound lock" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Mahoney · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lock_and_cottage_on_Aylesbury_Arm_of_Grand_Union_-_geograph.org.uk_-_112420.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>984</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Huai’an, Jiangsu, China</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Qiao Weiyue · <a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Diodorus Siculus credits engineers of Ptolemy II with a lock in Egypt about 274 BCE, but not a pound lock.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal<span>486 BCE–609 CE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=pound-lock">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
